speechtext:
The House resumed consideration of the motion of Mr. Miller:
That this House condemns the government for its failure to support the Canadian fishing industry, as demonstrated
(a)	by betraying the interests of Canadian fishermen in its international fisheries negotiations with the United States;
(b)	by the imposition of unconscionably high interest rates and other policies which have led to instability in the fishing industry and inadequate income protection for Canadian fishermen;
(c)	by its lack of action to devise and implement the long-promised revisions in policies regulating the industry; and
(d)	by its lack of action to enforce existing legislation protecting our fisheries.
